Aether: newtab/search/suggest cleanup

Newtab orphans and dead content, local search, topsites, Firefox Suggest, Merino, crossword, search telemetry, suggest items, urlbar engagement, provider dispatch, group labels, FOG about:glean, sponsor protection, data-submission infobar, leftover metrics, top-window hardening, AI window, login migration, addon tab notes, sponsored attribution.

Squashed from 22 units:

  [core/80-newtab-orphan-tests.patch]
  Aether: delete the newtab tests orphaned by the MARS/Pocket removals
  
  Delete the newtab tests orphaned by the MARS, Pocket and
  discovery-stream removals.
  
  Every test here imports a module that no longer exists, so they cannot
  run: DiscoveryStreamFeed.sys.mjs went with the MARS/discovery-stream
  work, TopStoriesFeed.sys.mjs with the Pocket work, and
  HighlightsFeed.sys.mjs with the Highlights section. The browser ones
  reached DiscoveryStreamFeed through the shared harness getter in
  head.js, which is why a scan of the individual files missed three of
  them.
  
  - Five browser tests: the activation window, the customize menu's
    discovery-stream content, the Highlights section, the Pocket
    "last LinkMenu", and the ohttp image fetcher.
  - test/unit/lib/{ActivityStream,DiscoveryStreamFeed}.test.js.
  - test_AboutHomeStartupCacheWorker.js, which staged a topstories.json
    startup cache.
  
  browser.toml and xpcshell.toml lose the matching entries, and head.js
  loses the DiscoveryStreamFeed getter, which no remaining test uses.
  
  [core/81-newtab-dead-content.patch]
  Aether: drop the dead newtab content components and rebuild the bundle
  
  Remove the discovery stream, sponsored card and highlight slot
  content components, and rebuild the newtab bundle.
  
  The activity-stream bundle is a committed build artifact: mach build
  copies it into browser.jar and never regenerates it. That left it a
  few patches behind -- it still carried the ADS_* action types that the
  MARS work deleted from common/Actions.mjs. So the components below
  were dead at runtime but still shipped, 1.29 MiB of them.
  
  Nothing renders a discovery stream any more. Base.jsx gated
  DiscoveryStreamBase and the devtools admin panel on
  `DiscoveryStream.config.enabled`, and the feed that populated that
  config was deleted, so the reducer's literal `config: { enabled:
  false }` is the only value it ever holds. Tracing every import from
  content-src/activity-stream.jsx, with that gate treated as dead, leaves
  46 unreachable modules:
  
  - DiscoveryStreamBase and DiscoveryStreamAdmin in full.
  - The sponsored/story card tree: AdBanner, AdBannerContextMenu,
    CardCarousel, CardGrid, CardSections, DSCard, DSContextFooter,
    DSEmptyState, DSImage, DSLinkMenu, Highlights, HorizontalRule,
    InterestPicker, Navigation, PersonalizedCard, PrivacyLink, PromoCard,
    ReportContent, SafeAnchor, SectionContextMenu, SectionFollowButton,
    SectionTitle, TopicsWidget.
  - The highlight slots only the old widgets container used:
    FollowSectionButtonHighlight, HighlightImage, HighlightPopoverBody,
    HighlightText, the OMCHighlight registry/slot pair,
    WidgetsFeatureHighlight, WidgetsRowFeatureHighlight.
  - Leftovers of features already gone: Spaces, the Nova InterestPicker,
    BackgroundsSection, WeatherForecast, the pre-registry Widgets.jsx and
    WidgetWrapper with their DnD hooks, selectLayoutRender and
    useReorderFlip.
  
  In Base.jsx this drops WithDsAdmin (which existed only to host the
  admin panel), the on-demand spoc lifecycle and its three dispatches,
  the spoc placeholder duration ping, and a discovery stream user-event
  telemetry dispatch on the mobile download highlight.
  
  The bundle goes from 1.29 MiB / 163 modules to 995 KiB / 120, and no
  longer contains ADS_*, AdBanner, DSCard or DiscoveryStreamBase.
  
  The stylesheets and their committed CSS artifacts are left alone: they
  are a separate build (sass) and a separate artifact, and pruning them
  would mean regenerating activity-stream.css, nova/activity-stream.css
  and bundled-renderer.css. What is left of the discovery-stream string
  surface -- the Pocket reducer in common/Reducers.sys.mjs and the
  TOP_SITES_SPONSORED_* action types -- is the store's shape, and the
  system side has to stop sending it first.
  
  [core/82-newtab-local-search.patch]
  Aether: search from the newtab box instead of handing off to the urlbar
  
  Search from the newtab box instead of handing off to the urlbar.
  
  The SEARCH external component (content-search-handoff-ui) already ships
  both modes: with handoff it renders a fake button that focuses the
  urlbar on click, without it a real input driven by
  ContentSearchUIController. Flip the default so typing stays in the
  newtab search box.
  
  [core/83-newtab-search-corners.patch]
  Aether: round the newtab search box and suggestions to the medium radius
  
  Round the newtab search box and its suggestion panel to the medium radius.
  
  The non-handoff search stacked a pill-shaped input
  (border-radius: circle under Nova) on top of a sharp-cornered legacy
  suggestion table. Use the medium rounded corners for both instead:
  
  - The host radius variable now resolves to --border-radius-medium, so
    the handoff button and the real input get the same corners. The
    Nova media-query override is redundant and goes away.
  - The suggestion table gets the same border-radius; its existing
    overflow:hidden clips the header, one-off and settings rows to it.
  
  The arrow submit button already used the medium radius on its outer
  corners, so it now lines up with the input.
  
  [core/84-no-sponsored-topsites.patch]
  Aether: remove the sponsored topsites pipeline
  
  Remove the sponsored topsites pipeline: Contile, SOV and TopSitesTelemetry.
  
  With the endpoints empty and the toggles off, nothing could fetch or
  display a sponsored tile any more; what was left was ~700 lines of
  machinery plus the telemetry around it. Now it is gone:
  
  - TopSitesFeed: the ContileIntegration fetcher (endpoint, cache prefs,
    blocklist, Nimbus gate) with its periodic refresh and search-engine
    change hook, the Share-of-Voice sampler and its SOV_UPDATED dispatch,
    the frec-boost spoc provider and its exposure event, the sponsored
    merge/cap/position code in getLinksWithDefaults, and the pin-index
    adjustment for fixed sponsored slots. Defaults come from remote
    settings or the local pref again, with no sponsored entries.
  - TopSitesTelemetry: the whole class. It only fed the dead newtab ping
    (display positions and fail reasons nobody reads).
  - Content: TopSite no longer dispatches sponsored/SPOC impression or
    click stats, ImpressionStats drops its flightId block, and the
    sponsor-info menu entry goes with the ABOUT_SPONSORED_TOP_SITES
    action and its SUMO page opener in PlacesFeed. Blocking a URL still
    works; it just stops maintaining a sponsor blocklist.
  - Store: the SOV_UPDATED action and slice, the two sponsored action
    types and the unread mayHaveSponsoredTopSites value are gone. The
    bundle shrinks from 995 to 982 KiB.
  - Prefs: the contile endpoint/enabled/positions defaults go. The
    showSponsoredTopSites default stays: enterprise policy and Nimbus
    targeting still name it, and with nothing behind it the toggle is
    simply inert.
  
  Deliberately left alone: the sponsored guards in the render paths
  (isSponsored checks, menu selection, the Sponsored label). They are
  inert conditions on data that can no longer occur, and touching drag,
  drop and pin logic for them would risk the live grid for no gain.
  
  [core/85-no-firefox-suggest.patch]
  Aether: remove Firefox Suggest
  
  Remove Firefox Suggest: the urlbar provider, its manager, and both fetch backends.
  
  Suggest is the last subsystem with a real fetch path: Merino over
  HTTPS and the Rust backend ingesting remote-settings records. The
  endpoints were already empty, so nothing could come back, but the
  whole machine was still there -- provider, manager, 20 feature and
  backend modules, the generated Rust binding, prefs, settings UI,
  enterprise policy and ~100 tests. Now:
  
  - Delete QuickSuggest (manager), UrlbarProviderQuickSuggest and its
    contextual opt-in, SuggestBackendMerino, SuggestBackendRust and the
    18 remaining private/ feature modules, plus the generated
    RustSuggest binding.
  - Unregister both providers. The muxer, view, shared and telemetry
    helpers compare provider names as string literals, so they go inert
    on their own; the muxer's lazy module getters are removed since they
    would throw on first access.
  - UrlbarInputBase no longer fires a Merino corroboration query when a
    search is picked. BrowserComponents.manifest loses the Suggest
    idle-startup init, and the FirefoxSuggest enterprise policy goes with
    the manager it awaited.
  - Prefs: the quicksuggest.* and suggest.quicksuggest.* defaults go
    from UrlbarPrefs and firefox.js, plus the Suggest-type feature
    gates (amp, mdn, yelp, wikipedia, market, sports, realtimeOptIn,
    importantDates, yelpRealtime, addons) and every merino.* default.
  - Settings: the Suggest section (enable, all/sponsored/online
    toggles, dismissed-suggestions restore) and its strings leave
    search.mjs and the ftl files; the address-bar header is always the
    plain one now.
  - Tests: the whole tests/quicksuggest tree, the ML/AI/preferences
    Suggest tests, the suggest-driven engagement cases, and every
    manifest entry that named them.
  
  MerinoClient.sys.mjs stays for one more patch: newtab weather still
  imports it until the Merino widgets go in 86. The muxer keeps
  comparing the retired provider name as a literal; those branches can
  never fire.
  
  Deliberately untouched: the suggest.* toggles for history, bookmarks
  and search suggestions (live providers), and Nimbus' FeatureManifest
  fallbackPref schema.
  
  [core/86-no-merino-widgets.patch]
  Aether: remove the Merino-powered newtab widgets
  
  Remove the Merino-powered newtab widgets: weather, picture of the day, sports and stocks.
  
  All four lived off Merino: live endpoints with real URLs sat in the
  pref config (world-cup teams/matches/live/watch-links, the daily
  picture feed), and the clients fetched on timers. Like Helium, Aether
  does not offer any of that, so the whole stack goes:
  
  - Feeds: WeatherFeed, SportsFeed, PictureOfTheDayFeed, StocksFeed and
    the TemporaryMerinoClientShim they shared, plus MerinoClient.sys.mjs
    itself -- the last fetch client in the tree -- and the now-unused
    GeolocationUtils (already gone with Suggest).
  - Render: the Widgets/Weather, SportsWidget, PictureOfTheDay and
    Stocks component trees, the classic Weather component (its branch
    never rendered under Nova anyway), and the dead ImpressionStats
    component with its tests.
  - Registry, store and prefs: the four registry entries and their pref
    consts, the Weather/PictureOfTheDay/SportsWidget/Stocks reducer
    slices and their 50+ action types, the PREF_CONFIG blocks (including
    the hardcoded Merino URLs) with the region helpers behind them, the
    mayHaveSponsoredTopSites-style unread values, and every related
    default in firefox.js.
  - UI: the widget toggles leave both customize panels and the Settings
    Home page; Base no longer computes anything weather/sports shaped.
    Blocking a URL keeps working, minus the sponsor bookkeeping.
  
  Stocks goes too: same remote-quote machine, different widget.
  
  The bundle goes from 982 to 730 KiB. Deliberately left: the
  sponsored guards in the topsites render paths (inert conditions, same
  reasoning as patch 84) and the crossword widget's Merino bundle-origin
  comment (that widget stays).
  
  [core/87-no-crossword-attribution.patch]
  Aether: remove the Crossword widget and the last attribution calls
  
  Remove the Crossword widget and the last attribution calls.
  
  The Crossword widget is a remote iframe pointed at Merino game hosts
  (allowlisted in the newtab CSP for staging and production). Same
  family as the other Merino widgets, so it goes the same way: component
  and test, registry entry with its endpoint resolver, the feed prefs
  (including the hardcoded production bundle URL), the customize and
  Settings toggles, and the frame-src allowlist in the prerender
  template and its committed artifacts.
  
  PartnerLinkAttribution was already a no-op shell; now the shell goes
  too, with its last callers (PlacesFeed's action handler, the urlbar
  topsites engagement hook, the newtab click dispatch), the action type
  and both prefs.
  
  Also fixed here: hasContentAreaWidgets did a hardcoded registry lookup
  for the removed weather widget and threw on every newtab render. It
  now just checks the registry, and the stale migration comment goes
  with it.
  
  The bundle goes from 730 to 711 KiB.
  
  [core/88-no-search-telemetry.patch]
  Aether: remove the search telemetry pipeline
  
  Remove the search telemetry pipeline: BrowserSearchTelemetry, SearchSERPTelemetry with its parent/child actors and the SERPCategorization backend, the v2 telemetry schema, and the SERP-telemetry browser and unit tests.
  
  Callers are unwired: the SERP init in BrowserGlue, the startup/shutdown category entries, the actor registration, and the dead lazy imports. SAP annotations that only fed telemetry counters are dropped; the sapSource plumbing that builds engine submission URLs is untouched.
  
  [core/89-no-empty-suggest-item.patch]
  Aether: drop the empty Suggest item left in Search settings
  
  Patch 85 removed the Firefox Suggest toggle from the location-bar group but left empty braces behind. That id-less item stamps a setting-control with no setting, which throws SettingNotDefinedError on about:preferences. Remove it.
  
  [core/90-no-urlbar-engagement-telemetry.patch]
  Aether: remove the urlbar engagement telemetry pipeline
  
  Remove the urlbar engagement telemetry pipeline end to end: the TelemetryEvent recorder class, the UrlbarTelemetryUtils helpers and the UrlbarChildTelemetry message-path collector, the engagement/bounce/exposure record calls at every input and view site, the parent/proxy/actor message chain (including the inert recordSearchMode/recordSearchForm shells), the dormant exposure-recording prefs and muxer setter, the legacy urlbar telemetry doc, and the engagement-telemetry test suites.
  Kept because functional: the sapSource plumbing for engine URLs, autofill Places bookkeeping, the row type attribute, and the hidden-exposure result filtering.
  
  [core/91-restore-provider-engagement-dispatch.patch]
  Aether: restore provider engagement dispatch without telemetry
  
  Patch 90 over-cut: the engagement recorder also dispatched provider notifications (onEngagement/onImpression/onSearchSessionEnd), which carry functional behavior (tip dismissal, history removal, onboarding counters). Restore that dispatch slim, without any recording: a notifyProviders path on the parent, child, proxy and actor (with toWire/fromWire across the message boundary), fired at pick, menu, dismissal, navigation and abandon points with the same selection types providers switch on. Recording stays deleted.
  
  [core/92-no-suggest-group-label.patch]
  Aether: drop the Suggest group label and harden the l10n cache
  
  Patch 85 removed the urlbar-group-firefox-suggest string but left three live references: two row-label returns and the prefetch entry. Opening the panel threw SettingNotDefined-style uncaught errors from L10nCache. Drop the references (those rows show no group header now) and harden L10nCache.add so one missing string logs instead of throwing.
  
  [core/93-no-fog-about-glean.patch]
  Aether: remove FOG calls and the about:glean page
  
  Remove the about:glean debug page (content, strings, jar and moz.build entries, about: mapping, redesign pref, test) and the remaining FOG calls in product code: the shutdown-time instantiate in BrowserGlue, the distribution clear, the background-task inits and the experiment mirroring plus the empty Glean-metrics shell in the background updater. The fog service itself and its test API stay until the Glean definitions block.
  
  [core/94-no-sponsor-protection.patch]
  Aether: remove the sponsored-link protection pipeline
  
  Sponsored newtab links no longer exist, so the whole sponsored-link pipeline is dead: the SponsorProtection module and its tabbrowser hooks and hover decoration, the sponsored branches in click, context-menu and init flows, the triggeringSponsoredURL attributes and options, the sponsor-protection prefs and tests, and the sponsored-session dead code plus its visit fields in History.cpp. Search-engine triggering attributes are untouched.
  
  [core/95-no-data-submission-infobar.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead data-submission infobar
  
  Remove the data-submission policy infobar: its notifier (the telemetry reporting policy) is long gone, so it could never show. Drops the script, its loader, jar and manifest entries, and its strings.
  
  [core/96-no-record-glean-metrics-leftover.patch]
  Aether: drop the leftover Glean-metrics call in background update
  
  Patch 93 removed the _recordGleanMetrics method but missed one of its three call sites, which threw at startup idle. Remove it.
  
  [core/97-harden-top-non-pb-window.patch]
  Aether: harden topNonPBWindow against the startup race
  
  getMostRecentNonPBWindow throws when no normal window exists yet, so an early tabs.query crashed instead of getting null as documented. Catch and return null.
  
  [core/98-no-aiwindow-telemetry-shells.patch]
  Aether: remove the AI window telemetry shells
  
  Remove the AI window telemetry shells end to end: the stub recorder modules (TelemetryManager, TelemetryUtils, AIWindowTelemetry, ClientErrorTelemetry, SmartWindowTelemetry, ToolUITelemetry), their call sites across models, actors, components and tools, the client-error relay, the starter/model telemetry hooks, the telemetry tests, prefs and build entries. The functional SmartFormFill decisions stay.
  
  [core/99-no-login-migration-pwmgr-telemetry.patch]
  Aether: remove logins, migration and password telemetry calls
  
  Remove the telemetry call sites whose recorders were already stubbed: the about:logins event dispatchers and actor relay, the migration wizard event sends and extra-args plumbing, the password-generation shown flag and its autocomplete hooks, and the orphaned password-manager telemetry tests and manifests.
  
  [core/100-no-usage-addon-tabnotes-telemetry.patch]
  Aether: remove usage, addon and tab-notes telemetry leftovers
  
  Remove the usage, addon and tab-notes telemetry leftovers: gut BrowserUsageTelemetry to its engagement-pref bumper (dropping tab tracking, URI counting, install telemetry and the dead tests and doc), remove the addon install/manage/suspicious-site recorders and their callers, strip the tab-note and theme telemetrySource/installSource threading, and cut the neqo Glean glue stubs.
  
  [core/101-no-sponsored-attribution-thirdparty-leftovers.patch]
  Aether: remove sponsored attribution plumbing and third-party-modules leftovers
  
  Remove the sponsored topsites attribution plumbing (the dead sendAttributionRequest flag from both topsites backends, the sponsored URL/ID payload writers and schema fields, and the no-op onEngagement/onImpression overrides) and the orphaned third-party-modules ping test, manifest entry and doc. The isSponsored display flag and its readers stay: they drive the sponsored badge and filtering, not telemetry.\n
